Browser evaluation at the working tree that became ab1723b (two cosmetic edits followed the
observations: one sentence of the workflow lede, and no focus outline on the h1). Chrome on macOS,
dark scheme, through the Claude in Chrome extension; values are from the live DOM and screenshots.
Two servers: this repository on 4877 (22 records) and a scratch repository on 4878 with one
iterative change carrying three ledger entries, two iterations (one with "<b>not a time</b>" as its
time), and a human decision by "<i>Ada</i>".

EVAL-004 the workflow view (#/workflow, #/workflow/verify)
  nav: Changes, Workflow; Workflow has aria-current="page"; title "Workflow · Soft Foundry"; h1 "Workflow".
  Sixteen phases in order, each "Required" or "Optional" in words; the four optional phases have a
    dashed edge as well. 06 verify selected from the URL.
  Panel for verify: skill, directory, model profile, "Then evaluate"; summary says it is a hardening
    phase and that its evidence is commit-bound; eleven checks, each with its description; files
    results.md, tests.yml, evidence/manifest.yml, handoff.yml.
  Selecting 13 review: hash #/workflow/review, focus stays on the button, facts include
    "Can return to remediate (on blocking findings)".
  Ways back: remediate to verify (always); observe to verify (when code changed); review to remediate
    (on blocking findings); judge to remediate (when the judgment is BLOCKED); judge to intake (when
    the judgment is REJECTED).
  Tracks: gated (default) and iterative with its exploring stage, what must be complete before a
    person vets it, and what is not required first; "A high risk change is always on the gated track."
  Judgments: the four verdicts.

