  #/change/ui-server/attack: each check shows its detail and "Checks: <description>".
  Timeline for ui-server: 19 events, oldest first, created then started/completed pairs, times as
    "2026-10-02 03:47 UTC". Spend: "No spend is recorded. Whoever runs a phase records it with
    soft-foundry budget record."
  #/change/costly (scratch): lede "Iterative track, exploring: 2 iterations recorded. Not yet vetted
    by a person."
    Timeline, six events: iteration 1, the decision, created, three spend entries. The iteration whose
    time is "<b>not a time</b>" is absent. The decision reads "... approved by <i>Ada</i>" as text.
    Spend: "Recorded $10.50 across 3 entries: 421000 tokens in, 48200 out. 1 entry has no cost."
    Policy line: cap $10.00 per change, $5.00 per phase, a person approves above $20.00.
    Note: "Over the cap for one change. Continuing is a financial commitment that needs a person's
    approval."
    Table: intake 120000 / 8000 / $6.40 / 1 / Over; implement ... $4.10 / 1 / Within; verify ...
    not priced / 1 / Unknown.
    Elements under <main> matching b, i, script, img: 0.
  An unknown change shows "No such change" with a way back.

EVAL-006 accessibility of the new parts
  Pause sets data-paused on the root and the stylesheet stops the gate animation under it; resuming
    removes it.
  New tables and lists: the spend table has a caption and scoped headers and sits in a focusable
    scroll region; the timeline is an ordered list; "Over", "Within", "Unknown" are words.
  No horizontal overflow of the page on either view at the window's width.
  Colours are the palette already measured in ui-server; no new colour was introduced.

Not exercised: a screen reader; the light scheme on screen; 200% zoom; a 320 px viewport for the new
views (the timeline collapses to one column under 40rem by rule, not observed).
